.TH "CSSTRANSFORMVALUE.TOMATRIX" "3JS" "September 10, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSTransformValue.toMatrix \- CSSTransformValue: toMatrix() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]toMatrix()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] interface returns a \f[CR]DOMMatrix\f[R]
object.
.PP
The returned matrix is the product of the matrices of each
\f[CR]CSSTransformComponent\f[R] in the \f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R],
computed by calling \f[CR]CSSTransformComponent.toMatrix()\f[R] on each
component in turn and multiplying the results together, in order.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toMatrix()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]DOMMatrix\f[R] object.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Raised if any lengths involved in generating the matrix are not
compatible units with px (such as relative lengths or percentages).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Converting a transform to a matrix
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] transform = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTransformValue([
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTranslate(CSS.px(10), CSS.px(20)),
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSScale(2, 3),
]);

\f[B]const\f[R] matrix = transform.toMatrix();
console.log(matrix.a, matrix.d); \f[I]// 2 3\f[R]
console.log(matrix.e, matrix.f); \f[I]// 10 20\f[R]
.EE
.SS Handling incompatible units
\f[CR]toMatrix()\f[R] throws if a component\(cqs length can\(cqt be
resolved to pixels, such as a percentage:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] transform = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTransformValue([
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTranslate(CSS.percent(50), CSS.px(20)),
]);

\f[B]try\f[R] {
  transform.toMatrix();
} \f[B]catch\f[R] (e) {
  console.log(e); \f[I]// TypeError\f[R]
}
.EE
